  // version 1.0.1
  // handbook
  "confession:handbook-introduction-ma-title": "Medieval Architecture Mod",
  "confession:handbook-introduction-ma-text": "Medieval Architecture adds archways, tiny windows, windowsills, leaded glass windows, gates, portcullises, drawbridges, big trapdoors and braziers. Most stone constructions are built step by step in the world: the material of each step decides how the result looks. The interaction help shows what to add next as soon as you hold a matching item.<br><br><strong>Archways</strong><br>Craft a construction frame and place it. Then add with <hk>ctrl</hk> + <hk>rightmouse</hk>: loose <a href=\"handbook://item-stone-granite\">stones</a> for the rim, <a href=\"handbook://item-mortar\">mortar</a> and finally a fill block, e.g. rock, cobblestone, stone bricks, polished rock, dry stone, plaster, wattle and daub, bricks, rammed earth or mud bricks. Rim and fill can be different materials, also from other mods. A finished archway can get a glass pane (window) or boards (door lintel for a door).<br><br><strong>Tiny windows and windowsills</strong><br>The recipe decides the rim stones. Place the block and finish it with a fill block, the same way as an archway. Tiny windows can get a glass pane afterwards.<br><br><strong>Gates, drawbridges and trapdoors</strong><br>They open and close like a vanilla door. While sneaking, every part can be reinforced with a <a href=\"handbook://item-plumbandsquare\">plumb and square</a> or locked with a padlock. All trapdoors and the small gate seal rooms, so a cellar closed with a trapdoor gets the cellar bonus. Gates and raised drawbridges hold back water.<br><br><strong>Brazier</strong><br>Assemble 4 <a href=\"handbook://item-confession:brazierpart\">brazier parts</a> and a metal hoop, place the empty brazier, add 3 pieces of firewood and light it. It burns much longer than a firepit.",

